{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1762","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Binary Strings are Fun"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A binary string$$$^\\dagger$$$ $$$b$$$ of odd length $$$m$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$b_i$$$ is the median$$$^\\ddagger$$$ of $$$b[1,i]^\\S$$$ for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" indices $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq i \\leq m$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a binary string $$$a$$$ of length $$$k$$$, a binary string $$$b$$$ of length $$$2k-1$$$ is an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extension"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$a$$$ if $$$b_{2i-1}=a_i$$$ for all $$$i$$$ such that $$$1 \\leq i \\leq k$$$. For example, "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"0"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"0"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extensions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1001"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". String $$$x=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1011011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extension"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of string $$$y=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1001"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" because $$$x_3 \\neq y_2$$$. Note that there are $$$2^{k-1}$$$ different "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extensions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$. Find the sum of the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extensions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" over all prefixes of $$$s$$$. In other words, find $$$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} f(s[1,i])$$$, where $$$f(x)$$$ gives number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extensions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of string $$$x$$$. Since the answer can be quite large, you only need to find it modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger$$$ A binary string is a string whose elements are either $$$\\mathtt{0}$$$ or $$$\\mathtt{1}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\ddagger$$$ For a binary string $$$a$$$ of length $$$2m-1$$$, the median of $$$a$$$ is the (unique) element that occurs at least $$$m$$$ times in $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\S$$$ $$$a[l,r]$$$ denotes the string of length $$$r-l+1$$$ which is formed by the concatenation of $$$a_l,a_{l+1},\\ldots,a_r$$$ in that order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$), where $$$n$$$ is the length of the binary string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains the binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n1\n1\n1\n0\n2\n11\n3\n010\n9\n101101111\n37\n1011011111011010000011011111111011111\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1\n3\n3\n21\n365\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first and second test cases, $$$f(s[1,1])=1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the answer is $$$f(s[1,1])+f(s[1,2])=1+2=3$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, the answer is $$$f(s[1,1])+f(s[1,2])+f(s[1,3])=1+1+1=3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$f(\\mathtt{11})=2$$$ because two "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extensions"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are possible: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"101"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$f(\\mathtt{01})=1$$$ because only one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"extension"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is possible: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"011"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1762C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1762/problem/C"}